ick LaLota (R) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term-plus incumbent Nick LaLota defends an R+4 Long Island seat against Suffolk County legislator Chris Gallant. LaLota has raised $4.5 million and holds a large cash advantage, while Gallant has raised $1.7 million, with a notable surge after viral headlines about leaked intimate photos drew attention to his campaign. The race has drawn little debate activity and Newsday made no endorsement.\n\nExpert ratings uniformly favor LaLota, ranging from Lean R to Solid R, and prediction markets price his win chances around 80%. The lone available poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from December, showed a narrow three-point race but is dated. The race looks like a Republican hold with modest but real Democratic upside in a favorable environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1953, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.158, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1553, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.188, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1399, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0851, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1487, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1542, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1035, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1186, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1205, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.124, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1216, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1197, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1405, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1018, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.1226, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0863, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.1244, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.1124, "margin": -